    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with an aggressive stance against Max Scherzer, positioning **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) as our cornerstone asset. **Henderson** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against a pitcher with a 5.10 xERA, and critically, Scherzer\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts **Henderson**'s stolen base probability, a priority given our league\u2019s scarcity. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.93) is a top-tier play; his matchup against Bassitt is bolstered by a +19% SP skill advantage and a favorable spot in the #3 hole. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (66.17) remains a must-start despite the lineup pending status, as he continues to be the primary engine for our power production.\n\nPlatoon edges and park factors are heavily influencing the fringes of today's lineup. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.53) sees a +14% bump due to the dynamic platoon advantage against McLean, while **Henry Bolte** (57.60) receives a massive +10% boost from park factors that offset his neutral platoon standing. The closest call on the bench was **Miguel Vargas** (51.09). While **Vargas** offers reliable contact and projected xwOBA upside, he ultimately ceded the utility spot to **Coby Mayo** (59.35). **Mayo** provides greater raw power potential against the struggling Scherzer, and even with a slight negative platoon adjustment, his ability to exploit the same slow-delivery dynamic as **Henderson** makes him the statistically superior play for Roto efficiency.\n\nRisk management remains a theme as we navigate several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Tommy White**, **Henry Bolte**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill**. We are proceeding with the assumption that **Merrill** occupies the #5 spot, where a +5% wind-out factor in his favor helps neutralize the -7% SP skill penalty against Anthony Molina. **Liam Hicks** (38.30) was evaluated but remained benched as he fell below our 40.0 floor, failing to provide enough upside against a tough matchup to justify a start. We will continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Andy Pages**, who remain sidelined on the IL, but the current configuration provides the highest ceiling for our 5x5 categories.",
